# Protocol package

- Pure Node/TS: no `vscode`, no git side effects. Defaults belong in parse/load (`courseDefaults`, `chapterDefaults`), not in the extension.
- Keep `schema.json` in sync with types; course/chapter are separate `$defs`. Authors set `$schema` on the JSONC file.
- Validate only structure/safety (paths, uniqueness). Existence of snapshot dirs is the extension’s job.
- Load: Open Course / `loadCourseFromFile` take a `course.jsonc` path. Directory lookup (`course.jsonc` then `.course-config/course.jsonc`) remains for cloned remotes and `isCourseRepository`.
- Optional `chaptersDir` (default `chapters`, relative to the directory that contains `course.jsonc`; no `..` or absolutes).
- Paths: reject `..` and absolutes for source/chapter-relative fields (`normalizeSourceDirPath` / relative file helpers).
- Update `fixtures/` + `tests/` with any behavior change. Empty/`{}` course.jsonc must still load via defaults.
- Export new helpers from `src/index.ts`. Pack before consumers run (`vp run @learn-by-diff/protocol#pack`).
